\verb{x_F = X[1] + X[k + 1] - (1 / log(2)) sum_\{i=0\}^\{k-1\} log(1 + 1 / (k + i)) X[k + i + 1]}, equivalently
\verb{X[1] + sum_\{i=0\}^\{k-1\} a[i] (X[k + 1] - X[k + i + 1])} with positive
weights \code{a[i] = log((k + i + 1) / (k + i)) / log(2)} summing to one
(Fraga Alves & Neves 2014; Fraga Alves, Neves & Rosario 2016, equations 6
and 7). It uses the \verb{2k} largest observations and is never below the
sample maximum. It is consistent for \code{gamma <= 0} and diverges for
\code{gamma > 0} (Fraga Alves et al. 2016, Proposition 1).
}
\details{
